{{!--
	One row of the classic Advantages block on the Attributes tab (stats_features.hbs).

	usedots=true	Backgrounds / Other Traits - an editable dot row driven by the item's own
					system.value / system.max. No JavaScript of its own: SetupDotCounters_v2 fills
					the dots at render time and OnDotCounterChange persists a click back to
					system.value on the embedded item, both keyed on data-* attributes only.
	usedots=false	Merits / Flaws - the item's point value, read from system.level and falling back
					to system.value, because the two producers of these items disagree about which
					field carries the number: the compendium exporter writes the cost/bonus into
					system.level and leaves value at 0, while the character exporter hard-codes
					level to "0" and writes the rating into system.value. The number is never
					signed or negated - the Flaws heading is what marks it as points gained.
					Both candidates go through the `pointValue` helper (module/handlebars.js), NOT
					`gt`: the point value is not always a number - 88 merits/flaws carry the range,
					either/or or tier list the book prints ("1 a 5", "1 o 3", "1/2/3/4/5") and core's
					`gt` coerces those to NaN, which rendered an empty box. `pointValue` keeps the
					0-shows-nothing rule for numeric values and passes any other string through
					verbatim. Do NOT drop the system.value candidate - it is the character
					exporter's only field.
	useroll=true	Backgrounds AND Other Traits - makes the row's NAME a roll target: vrollable plus
					data-action="rollDice" + data-rollitem="true" + data-itemid +
					data-object="wod.types.background", which reaches the background branch of
					ActionHelper.RollDialog and opens the same DialogGeneralRoll an ability name
					opens (rating pre-filled, Attribute picked in the dialog). Same parameter name
					and meaning stats.hbs already passes to stats_abilities.hbs. Not gated on
					locked - rolling mutates nothing, exactly as ability names are rollable on a
					locked sheet. No data-type: RollDialog reads dataset.type only on the frenzy
					path (action-helpers.js:475,478).

	INVARIANT: the roll sits on the NAME div and editDot sits on the dot spans inside
	.resource-value - two SIBLINGS, neither an ancestor of the other, with no data-action on any
	ancestor of either. That is the whole reason a dot click cannot roll and a name click cannot
	write a rating; ApplicationV2 dispatches to the nearest [data-action] ancestor and this system
	overrides no dispatch. stats_abilities.hbs has the identical shape. Do not nest one inside the
	other.

	add-pc-sheet-v3 §8.5 — PORTED FROM `feature_item.hbs`. Backgrounds/Merits/Flaws/Other Traits
	used to render on BOTH the Stats tab (here) and the Features tab, from one
	`prepareAdvantageLists` call — a rendering duplicate. This partial is the copy that survived,
	because it is the ONLY place either sheet lets a player EDIT one of these four kinds' rating
	(the dot row two blocks below, or the point number); `feature_item.hbs` has only ever printed a
	read-only number for them. So what THAT partial had and this one lacked — drag-reorder, the
	`isactive` toggle, and send-to-chat — is added below, verbatim in markup and action wiring
	(`.draggable`/`itemActive`/`sendChat` are read by the SAME global binders/action map either
	partial's markup triggers; nothing new was registered). `edittitle`/`deletetitle` are new
	required params, one pair per caller in `stats_features.hbs`, same strings `feature_item.hbs`
	already used for these items on the Features tab.

	This partial has exactly ONE caller (`stats_features.hbs`), unlike `feature_item.hbs`'s twelve —
	which is why the port landed here rather than the other way around: retrofitting an editable dot
	column into a partial twelve other blocks share, to make IT the survivor instead, would have put
	Merits/Bloodbounds/Boons/Connections/... at risk for a decision that only concerns four of them.
--}}
<div class="clearareaBox" data-itemid="{{item._id}}">

	{{!-- Drag-reorder handle + the isactive toggle, ported from `feature_item.hbs`'s row (its
	      `.width-iconbox draggable` grip and `.item-active` checkbox) — same classes, same
	      `data-action`, so the same generic binders (`_setupDragAndDrop`'s `.draggable` sweep,
	      `itemActive` in `DEFAULT_OPTIONS.actions`) pick them up with nothing new registered. Both
	      sit to the LEFT of the description eye, matching that partial's own left-to-right order. --}}
	<div class="pullLeft width-iconbox draggable"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-grip-vertical"></i></div>

	{{#if (isChecked item.system.isactive)}}
		<i class="pullLeft item-active pointer icon fa-regular fa-square-check" title="{{localize 'wod.power.active'}}" data-itemid="{{item._id}}" data-type="isactive" data-action="itemActive"></i>
	{{else}}
		<i class="pullLeft item-active pointer icon fa-regular fa-square" title="{{localize 'wod.power.active'}}" data-itemid="{{item._id}}" data-type="isactive" data-action="itemActive"></i>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- The description eye, to the LEFT of the name. This block had no icon column at all, so
	      the right-hand side is already spoken for by the dot row / point box.

	      It is a SIBLING of the name div, never a child: the name carries
	      data-action="rollDice" and ApplicationV2 dispatches to the nearest [data-action]
	      ancestor, so an eye nested inside it would roll the Background on every click. The
	      collapsible is bound by addEventListener in _bindCollapsibleButtons (it has no
	      data-action of its own), which is why placing it here cannot disturb the invariant this
	      file documents above.

	      Not gated on `locked` — reading a description mutates nothing, the same reason the name
	      stays rollable on a locked sheet, and the same choice list_icons.hbs makes by keeping its
	      tooltip block outside its own locked check.

	      Always clickable now (open-item-window-from-eye-icon): the click opens the item's own
	      sheet in a window, so there is no "nothing to show" case any more - the item's other
	      fields (name, type, ratings, ...) are visible even when system.description is empty. --}}
	<i class="pullLeft pointer icon collapsible button fa-solid fa-eye"
		title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.description'}}"
		data-itemid="{{item._id}}"></i>

	{{!-- The name is a roll target when `useroll` is passed AND the item carries no pool of its
	      own. The `dice1` guard is what makes it safe to pass `useroll` for Other Traits as well
	      as Backgrounds — see this file's header for why that was deferred, and why the deferral
	      no longer applies:

	      `data-rollitem="true"` reaches a chain of `dataset.object` branches in
	      ActionHelper.RollDialog that ENDS IN `ui.notifications.error("Item Roll missing
	      function")` (action-helpers.js:423). So emitting it with the background object on an item
	      that should roll its own dice1/dice2 pool would not degrade gracefully — it would roll
	      the wrong pool. An item that HAS its own pool therefore keeps the plain, unrollable name
	      here and stays rollable from the Features tab, where `feature_item.hbs` already rolls it
	      properly. Measured on the live world: 11 of 11 rows in this column are `Feature` with no
	      `dice1`, so today every one of them takes the rollable branch. --}}
	{{#if useroll}}
		{{#if item.system.dice1}}
			<div class="pullLeft ability-headlineWidth headlineNormal"
				title="{{item.name}}">{{shorten item.name 20}}</div>
		{{else}}
			<div class="pullLeft vrollable ability-headlineWidth headlineNormal"
				title="{{item.name}}"
				data-action="rollDice"
				data-rollitem="true"
				data-itemid="{{item._id}}"
				data-object="wod.types.background">{{shorten item.name 20}}</div>
		{{/if}}
	{{else}}
		<div class="pullLeft ability-headlineWidth headlineNormal"
			title="{{item.name}}">{{shorten item.name 20}}</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- Send-to-chat / edit / delete, ported from `feature_item.hbs`'s `.iconBox` (which includes
	      this exact partial, `list_icons.hbs`). Placed BEFORE the value/dots block below so the
	      float order comes out value-then-icons left to right (the first `pullRight` in source ends
	      up rightmost). `showtooltip=false`: this row already has its own description eye above,
	      and rendering `list_icons.hbs`'s eye too would be a second, redundant one. --}}
	<div class="pullRight">
		{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/list_icons.hbs" showsendchat=true showedit=true showdelete=true showtooltip=false item=item locked=locked edittitle=edittitle deletetitle=deletetitle}}
	</div>

	{{#if usedots}}

		<div class="pullRight resource-value"
			data-itemid="{{item._id}}"
			data-value="{{item.system.value}}"
			data-name="system.value">

			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/stat_value_dots.hbs"
				max=item.system.max
				value=item.system.value
				locked=locked
				name="system.value"
				itemid=item._id
				dotType=config.sheettype.mortal}}

		</div>

	{{else}}

		<div class="pullRight notes-valueBox centerText headlineNormal">
			{{#if (pointValue item.system.level item.system.value)}}
				{{pointValue item.system.level item.system.value}}
			{{else}}
				&nbsp;
			{{/if}}
		</div>

	{{/if}}

</div>
{{!-- The inline .description panel that used to live here (toggled by the eye above) is removed:
      the eye now opens the item's own sheet in a window, where the description is visible whether
      or not it is empty. The data-itemid on the eye above deliberately MATCHES the Features tab's
      copy of this item; that used to matter for tab-scoping the old inline toggle, but
      item.sheet.render(true) is inherently idempotent (raises the same window), so no scoping is
      needed any more. --}}
